   "text": "You tend to forget that because agents are doing everything for you, some of those things could be deterministic, but after you run a session for like three, four, seven hours, you're exhausted. Last thing you want is you think about what could this be a linter? What could this be a custom rule? You just forget. So I built a command called slash retro looking at the last session or the current session you just had. and figured out what is it that you had to course correct the agent. So what this slash retro command does is interviews you. And at the end, this is a table of everything that could be made deterministic now. Maybe I could do a custom linting rule to prevent writing test this way, writing code this way. If you were to try now, it could be as simple as you are a... an agent specialized in helping me reflect and find optimizations for my development workflow. Look into my previous session or my current session, interview me, use Socratic method, find the threads until there's nothing left. Then create a table showing what exactly could be made deterministic. That's basically what wetter is, it's like 30 lines. If I'm honest.",
